From 885c716e71b326aa1569764fb57d40ec7020b561 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mpenelange <191051681+mpenelange@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 23:26:18 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] MIPS: Octeon: AES (ecb, cbc, ctr) and GHASH on the crypto unit

Register aes, ecb(aes), cbc(aes), ctr(aes) and ghash backed by the OCTEON
COP2 AES unit and Galois field multiplier, so the kernel's gcm/rfc4106
and authenc templates (IPsec ESP) run on hardware. Modelled on the COP2
usage in Cavium's cavium_ipsec_kame; correctness is left to the crypto
self-tests (an implementation that fails them is not used).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
